# FORGE Agent Guide

PostgreSQL-only. **Package: `forgex`** (import as `forge`). [Docs](https://tryforge.dev/docs) | `forge --help`

## Verify Changes

```bash
cargo clippy --all-targets -- -D warnings && cargo test --features embedded-db && bun lint && bun format
```

## Testing (In-File with Embedded DB)

Tests live in same file as function. Use `#[cfg(all(test, feature = "embedded-db"))]` to gate.

```rust
// src/functions/create_user.rs
use forge::prelude::*;

#[forge::mutation(public)]
pub async fn create_user(ctx: MutationContext, args: CreateUserArgs) -> Result<User> {
    // ... implementation
}

#[cfg(all(test, feature = "embedded-db"))]
mod tests {
    use super::*;
    use forge::testing::{IsolatedTestDb, TestDatabase};
    use std::path::Path;

    async fn setup_db(test_name: &str) -> (IsolatedTestDb, sqlx::PgPool) {
        let base = TestDatabase::embedded().await.unwrap();
        let db = base.isolated(test_name).await.unwrap();
        db.run_sql(forge::FORGE_INTERNAL_SQL).await.unwrap();  // Forge internals
        db.migrate(Path::new("migrations")).await.unwrap();    // Your migrations
        (db, db.pool().clone())
    }

    #[tokio::test]
    async fn test_creates_user() {
        let (_db, pool) = setup_db("creates_user").await;

        // Use runtime queries (not macros) for test flexibility
        sqlx::query("INSERT INTO users (id, email) VALUES ($1, $2)")
            .bind(Uuid::new_v4()).bind("test@test.com")
            .execute(&pool).await.unwrap();

        let count: (i64,) = sqlx::query_as("SELECT COUNT(*) FROM users")
            .fetch_one(&pool).await.unwrap();
        assert_eq!(count.0, 1);
    }
}
```

Run: `cargo test --features embedded-db`

## Function Selection

| Need | Use | Note |
|------|-----|------|
| Read data | Query | Cacheable, subscribable |
| Write data | Mutation | Transactional, triggers reactivity |
| External API | Action | Has `ctx.http()` |
| Async work | Job | Retryable, progress tracking |
| Scheduled | Cron | Time-based, leader-only |
| Multi-step | Workflow | Durable, compensatable |

## Backend Patterns

```rust
ctx.db()                          ctx.require_user_id()?
ctx.dispatch_job(name, args)      ctx.start_workflow(name, input)

#[forge::query]                  // + cache="30s", public, rate_limit(...)
#[forge::mutation]               // + timeout=30, require_role("admin")
#[forge::action]                 // + timeout=60
#[forge::job]                    // + #[retry(...)], #[priority], #[idempotent]
#[forge::cron("0 * * * *")]      // + #[timezone], #[catch_up]
#[forge::workflow]               // + #[version], #[timeout]
```

## Anti-Patterns

| Don't | Do |
|-------|-----|
| External API in Mutation | Use Action |
| `tokio::sleep` in Workflow | `ctx.sleep()` |
| Destructure `$props()` | Keep reference |
| Poll with `query()` loop | `subscribe()` |
| `ctx.auth.user_id().unwrap()` | `ctx.require_user_id()?` |

## Schema

```rust
#[forge::model]
pub struct Task { pub id: Uuid, pub status: TaskStatus }

#[forge::forge_enum]
pub enum TaskStatus { Pending, Completed }
```

## Run

```bash
[ -f .env ] || cp .env.example .env
docker compose up --build
```

## Structure

```
src/functions/  # One file per function (+ tests inside)
src/schema/     # #[forge::model]
migrations/     # NNNN_name.sql (-- @up / -- @down)
```

## Workflow

Schema → Migration → `forge add <type> <name>` → Register in main.rs → `forge generate`

## Auth

```rust
#[forge::query(public)]                    // No auth
#[forge::mutation(require_role("admin"))]  // Role required
ctx.require_user_id()?                      // Uuid or error
```

## Frontend (Svelte 5)

```svelte
const users = subscribe(getUsers, {});     // Real-time
await mutate(createUser, { name });        // Write
```

**NEVER edit `frontend/src/lib/forge/`** — auto-generated.

## Code Quality

Idiomatic Rust | Small functions | Fail fast | No premature abstraction | Use `bun` only
